<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ROUX Sports launcher icon: the with-SPORTS artwork variant from the supplied brand pack.

  This is a deliberate A/B against the plain RX icon (PR #31). The word SPORTS is the reason: at 48 dp it
  measures roughly three pixels of cap height, so it is likely to read as a smudge rather than a word. The
  artwork is composited exactly as the plain variant was, so the only difference on the home screen is the
  wordmark - which is what makes the two comparable by eye rather than by argument.

  Deliberately unqualified (`mipmap-anydpi`, not `-v26`): minSdk is 31, so every supported platform
  understands adaptive icons and a v26 qualifier would be dead configuration (lint's ObsoleteSdkInt
  flags exactly that).

  The foreground is a bitmap because the pack ships no vector master for the RX mark - only the
  wordmark has one. Two consequences, both deliberate:

  * The artwork keeps its own dark field, so the background colour matches it exactly (Carbon Black) and
    the foreground's edge is faded out rather than cut. A plain inset crop leaves a visible square seam
    inside the launcher mask; the fade is what removes it.

  * There is no monochrome layer, so the icon is not themeable on Android 13+. Keying a silhouette out
    of this raster does not work: the monogram's X is part white and part orange, so a luminance key
    truncates it, and widening the key drags in the orange speed trails that cross the field. Every
    variant tried produced a mark that reads as something other than RX at 48 dp. Faking one would put
    a wrong logo on the home screen; a vector master from design is the real fix, and until it exists
    the icon is simply not themeable.

  MonochromeLauncherIcon is suppressed for that reason and only for this file. The follow-up is a
  vector RX mark, at which point the layer is derived from paths rather than pixels.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:ignore="MonochromeLauncherIcon">
    <background android:drawable="@color/ic_launcher_background" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground" />
</adaptive-icon>
